Creating a Git branch and a pull request step by step.

1️⃣ Create a new branch

From your project root, run:

git checkout -b feature/TW-186
checkout -b → creates a new branch and switches to it.

feature/TW-186 → your branch name.

2️⃣ Make your changes

Edit your files as needed. Then stage and commit:

git add .
git commit -m "TW-186: Your commit message here"
3️⃣ Push the branch to remote

git push origin feature/TW-186
This uploads your branch to GitHub (or your Git remote).

4️⃣ Create a Pull Request (PR)

You have two options:

Option A: Using GitHub website

Go to your repository on GitHub.

You should see a prompt: “Compare & pull request” for your new branch.

Click it → fill title/description → create PR.

Option B: Using GitHub CLI (if installed)

gh pr create --base main --head feature/TW-186 --title "TW-186: Your title" --body "Description of changes"
--base main → the branch you want to merge into (often main or develop).

--head feature/TW-186 → your branch.

After this, your branch is on GitHub and the PR is ready for review. ✅

